From a5b00ea95e48977e175369bd8014aa898c0238c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tp2-lane <tp2-lane@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:15:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: a prompt pass a chunk a round, several passes at a
 time, shortest first

Upstream a27d2f00 runs a prompt pass in pieces between rounds but admits one
pass at a time: a request that arrives during a long cold pass waits for that
pass to end (measured 27.9 s behind 44K tokens). This re-ports patch 0005's
scheduling onto that structure.

- Engine.filling is a list: addStream opens a piece for every arrival, and
  fillStream advances the pass its caller picked; fillNext takes the fewest
  prompt rows left (Stream.fill_at, set by a backend that fills in pieces),
  oldest of equals, and fill_patience makes every pass advance in turn.
- addStream opens a piece even when no stream decodes: upstream ran a lone
  pass whole inside its admission, which blocks every arrival behind it.
- LaneHost admits while passes fill, keeps its own filling list, and picks
  among them with the same rule.
- Lanes keeps one Fill per slot (its spans and rows parked with it) and
  switches the model's fill state between them, re-sending fill_begin and the
  images; the KV rows stay in the pool, so a switch costs a frame, not a pass.
